  "narrative": "No claims are due for assessment. I registered targeted refinements of the three major accepted associations, prioritizing the unresolved lineage-context signal for SMARCA4-loss and clarifying co-loss context effects. The first three proposals ask whether the reversed lineage interaction H94 is robust in a cleaner TP53-/KEAP1-intact background: adenocarcinoma and squamous SMARCA4-loss main effects plus a lineage interaction. For negative-direction SMARCA4-loss main effects, a positive signed estimate means lower raw dependency_composite in SMARCA4-loss versus intact, i.e. stronger composite dependency. For the +1 lineage interaction, a positive signed estimate means the adenocarcinoma SMARCA4-loss contrast is more positive/less negative than the squamous contrast, i.e. an attenuated SMARCA4-loss dependency effect in adenocarcinoma if the raw main effects remain negative. The KEAP1-loss lineage proposals similarly quantify adenocarcinoma and squamous effects in TP53-/SMARCA4-intact backgrounds and test whether lineage modification is null after removing co-loss confounding; for +1 KEAP1 main effects, positive signed estimates mean higher raw dependency_composite, i.e. weaker composite dependency. The co-loss conditional effects directly test whether TP53-loss, SMARCA4-loss, and KEAP1-loss retain their expected directions within the context of one of the other major losses, especially the suggestive but unresolved TP53-by-KEAP1 relationship. Finally, non-Avana library checks test whether the very large SMARCA4 and KEAP1 marginal associations are robust outside the dominant Avana library population. These are internal dataset associations only and do not establish causality, single-gene knockout behavior, biological pathway mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted core associations after validation/robustness: TP53-loss -> higher dependency_composite/weaker composite dependency; SMARCA4-loss -> lower dependency_composite/stronger composite dependency; KEAP1-loss -> higher dependency_composite/weaker composite dependency. H44 SMARCA4-loss marginal association accepted/closed with independent validation; H55 KEAP1-loss accepted/validated and active for context; H7 TP53-loss accepted/validated and active for context. Key unresolved: H94 reversed SMARCA4-by-lineage interaction has positive point estimate +0.211 [0.063,0.359] but lower bound below threshold, suggesting attenuated SMARCA4-loss effect in adenocarcinoma versus squamous. New proposals register TP53/KEAP1-intact lineage-restricted SMARCA4 main effects and interaction to test this. KEAP1 lineage interaction H78 overall rejected; new TP53/SMARCA4-intact lineage-restricted KEAP1 effects and interaction test whether that null is robust in cleaner backgrounds. New conditional co-loss tests: TP53-loss within KEAP1-loss, SMARCA4-loss within KEAP1-loss, KEAP1-loss within SMARCA4-loss, to clarify H31 and residual context effects. Non-Avana SMARCA4 and KEAP1 checks test library robustness beyond dominant Avana. Technical checks still active: high Cas9 KEAP1 H72, screen ROC interactions H75/H76, screen_nnmd main effects H85/H86 and TP53 H36/H37. Guardrails: composite endpoint; associations only; independent validation indicates internal robustness but not mechanism, causality, or external generalizability."
